\f0\fs53\fsmilli26667 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Context Intelligence Reference Architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs42\fsmilli21333 \cf2 1. Purpose\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 This document defines the 
\f1\b frozen reference architecture
\f0\b0  for a Context Intelligence Platform. It is intended to guide system architects, engineers, and product teams in building a production-grade, local-first system that provides shared organizational context across enterprise tools without orchestrating or controlling business processes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs42\fsmilli21333 \cf2 2. Architectural Objectives\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sa47\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf3 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Eliminate context silos across enterprise systems\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Preserve existing systems of record\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Provide ownership, freshness, trust, and activity awareness\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Remain advisory, explainable, and non-intrusive\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Be deployable locally / on\uc0\u8209 prem first\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Minimize dependence on LLMs\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs42\fsmilli21333 \cf2 3. High-Level Architecture (Frozen)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 Layered View\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sa47\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 1.
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Source Systems Layer (Read-only)\
2.
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Ingestion & Observation Layer\
3.
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Signal Extraction & Enrichment Layer\
4.
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Context Graph Layer (Core)\
5.
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Trust, Freshness & Confidence Layer\
6.
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Intelligence & Reasoning Layer\
7.
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Interaction Layer\
8.
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Governance & Control Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf3 Each layer is independently evolvable and communicates through events or well-defined APIs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs42\fsmilli21333 \cf2 4. Layer Responsibilities\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 4.1 Source Systems Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sa47\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf3 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 ERP, CRM, HRMS\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Ticketing systems\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Email & chat tools\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Local / shared file systems\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Wikis and document repositories\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf3 Constraints:
\f0\b0  - Read-only access - No workflow execution - No data ownership transfer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 4.2 Ingestion & Observation Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32 \cf3 Responsibilities:
\f0\b0  - Observe changes and activity - Normalize inputs into events - Provide reliable temporal ordering\

\f1\b Outputs:
\f0\b0  - Normalized events (create, modify, access, reference)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 4.3 Signal Extraction & Enrichment Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32 \cf3 Responsibilities:
\f0\b0  - Convert events into signals - Detect references, mentions, and relationships - Enrich with semantic and temporal hints\

\f1\b Signals include:
\f0\b0  - Activity signals - Relationship signals - Lifecycle signals - Parallel-work signals\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 4.4 Context Graph Layer (Core)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 The graph is the authoritative representation of organizational context.\

\f1\b Design Principles:
\f0\b0  - Append-only - Temporal - Explainable - Relationship-first\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 4.5 Trust, Freshness & Confidence Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32 \cf3 Responsibilities:
\f0\b0  - Compute freshness scores - Infer ownership confidence - Detect conflicts and duplicates - Produce reliability signals\

\f1\b Outputs:
\f0\b0  - Confidence metrics, never data changes\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 4.6 Intelligence & Reasoning Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32 \cf3 Components:
\f0\b0  - Deterministic rule engine - Graph traversal & reasoning - Lightweight LLM (optional, last-mile only)\

\f1\b Responsibilities:
\f0\b0  - Answer contextual questions - Perform impact analysis - Generate explanations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 4.7 Interaction Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32 \cf3 Interfaces:
\f0\b0  - Context-aware search - Natural language Q&A - Embedded context panels - Read-only APIs\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 4.8 Governance & Control Layer\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sa47\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf3 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Role-based access control\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Context-aware permissions\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Full audit trail\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Explainability support\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 Local-first deployment constraints\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs42\fsmilli21333 \cf2 5. Explicit Non-Goals (Locked)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li960\fi-480\sa47\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs32 \cf3 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 No workflow orchestration\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 No business process automation\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 No system-of-record replacement\

\f2 \'e1
\f3\fs18\fsmilli9333 \'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0\'a0 
\f0\fs32 No core dependency on external workflow tools (e.g., n8n)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs53\fsmilli26667 \cf2 6. Exact Context Graph Schema\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs42\fsmilli21333 \cf2 6.1 Node Types\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 Artifact\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 Represents any informational object.\
Properties: - artifact_id (stable) - artifact_type (doc, record, ticket, email, file) - source_system - title / name - created_at - last_modified_at - lifecycle_state (active, dormant, obsolete, superseded)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 Person\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 Properties: - person_id - name - role - team - org_unit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 System\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 Properties: - system_id - system_type - system_name\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 Concept\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 Represents abstract organizational concepts.\
Properties: - concept_id - concept_type (project, customer, product, policy) - name\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 Activity\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 Properties: - activity_id - activity_type (create, edit, review, discuss, approve) - timestamp\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

\fs37\fsmilli18667 \cf2 Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf3 Properties: - decision_id - decision_type (explicit, inferred) - timestamp - rationale (optional)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa106\partightenfactor0

